.TH STCC 1 "2026-10-17" "stcc 0.4.0"
.SH NAME
stcc \- freestanding C subset and Devpac assembler for Atari ST
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stcc
.RI [ options ] " input.c input.s input.o ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
stcc runs on Linux and emits relocatable TOS executables or fixed-address raw
ROM images for the original
Motorola 68000. It includes its own assembler and linker and needs no Atari libc.
This release supports integer C89 including int bit fields. It does not
implement complete ANSI C89: floating point, K&R definitions, and by-value
aggregate arguments/results are unavailable.
.PP
The __interrupt__ function specifier saves all data/address registers and
returns with RTE. The __naked__ specifier emits only the user assembly body.
Both require void (void). See INTERRUPTS.md for entry contracts and examples.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Select output file (default a.TOS, or a.rom with --rom).
.TP
.BI \-I " directory"
Add a C include search directory.
.TP
.BI \-D " NAME[=VALUE]"
Define a C preprocessor macro.
.TP
.B \-E
Preprocess C only.
.TP
.B \-S
Emit Devpac assembly.
.TP
.B \-c
Emit an internal STCO v1 object.
.TP
.B \-\-nostartfiles
Omit startup, stack and arithmetic support, also in ROM mode.
.TP
.B \-\-rom
Link a raw ROM image instead of a TOS executable. The default startup targets
the original ST with at least 512 KiB in RAM bank zero, reserves a screen at
0x78000, copies DATA to RAM, clears BSS and calls main in supervisor mode with
hardware IRQs masked. It provides no TOS services. Returning from main stops
the CPU with D0 holding the result. Requires linking; incompatible with -E/-S/-c.
.TP
.BI \-\-rom\-base " number"
ROM address (default 0xfc0000). Layout options require --rom.
.TP
.BI \-\-rom\-size " number"
ROM byte count (default 196608), padded with 0xff.
.TP
.BI \-\-ram\-base " number"
Writable DATA address (default 0x1000); BSS follows DATA.
.TP
.BI \-\-ram\-limit " number"
Exclusive upper DATA/BSS address (default 0x78000). Numbers are decimal or
0x-prefixed hexadecimal; addresses and sizes must be even. Non-default ROM
address/size or a RAM limit above 0x78000 require a custom --nostartfiles bootstrap.
.TP
.BI \-\-entry " symbol"
Assert entry symbol at the first TEXT byte; does not synthesize a reset vector.
.TP
.BI \-\-map " file"
Write symbol map.
.TP
.BI \-\-data-dir " directory"
Select runtime/include support root.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STCC_DATA
Runtime/include root, unless overridden by --data-dir.
.SH FILES
See README.md, ROM.md and docs under the installed share/stcc directory for the ABI,
inline assembly contract, supported Devpac syntax and known limitations.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, nonzero on a diagnostic. Target programs pass main's low
16 return bits to GEMDOS Pterm.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stmkdisk (1)
